{"step_index":3294,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T17:10:17Z","thinking":"The primary constraint is model availability; a fallback model must be selected. User intent highlights a need for parallel processing capability within the architecture. The focus shifts to identifying components facilitating concurrent operations, aiming for simultaneous file uploads.\n\n\nThe current implementation processes files sequentially, leading to excessive delays. Parallelism is crucial; concurrent workers should handle file uploads and processing to minimize overall time. The goal is to avoid waiting for individual file completion before initiating the next file's upload, drastically reducing the turnaround time.\n\n\nImplementing concurrent file uploads is confirmed. Each file will be assigned to a separate worker thread to allow parallel processing. A critical requirement is fault tolerance; a single file failure must not halt the processing of other files.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"D:\\\\miniconda3\\\\envs\\\\venv\\\\Lib\\\\site-packages\\\\unstructured_transform_client\\\\_client.py\"","EndLine":"340","StartLine":"275","toolAction":"\"Viewing client.extract.from_document\"","toolSummary":"\"Inspect from_document in client.py\""}}]}
{"step_index":3295,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T17:10:25Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T20:10:25+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T20:10:25+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///D:/miniconda3/envs/venv/Lib/site-packages/unstructured_transform_client/_client.py`\nTotal Lines: 421\nTotal Bytes: 17222\nShowing lines 275 to 340\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n275:         file_id: str | None = None,\n276:         filename: str | None = None,\n277:         schema: dict[str, Any],\n278:         prompt: str | None = None,\n279:         profile: str | None = None,\n280:         wait_seconds: int | None = None,\n281:     ) -> Any:\n282:         \"\"\"Extract directly from a document, in one call.\n283: \n284:         The multipart variant of POST /api/v2/extract. Reconstructed over the\n285:         generated transport because openapi-generator emits only the JSON body\n286:         for this path — see this module's docstring.\n287: \n288:         Takes a document OR the id of one already uploaded, exactly as\n289:         parse.run does: ExtractDocumentRequest declares both `input` and\n290:         `file_id`, so requiring the bytes would have made an already-uploaded\n291:         file unusable here and forced a needless re-upload. `filename` only\n292:         applies to the `file_id` path — a raw `input` upload already carries\n293:         its own name.\n294:         \"\"\"\n295:         if (input is None) == (file_id is None):\n296:             raise ValueError(\"pass exactly one of input or file_id\")\n297:         if input is not None and filename is not None:\n298:             raise ValueError(\"filename only applies to file_id; input already carries its name\")\n299: \n300:         return post_multipart(\n301:             self._client,\n302:             path=\"/api/v2/extract\",\n303:             file_field=\"input\",\n304:             file_value=None if input is None else as_file_part(input),\n305:             fields={\n306:                 \"file_id\": file_id,\n307:                 \"filename\": filename,\n308:                 \"schema\": json.dumps(schema),\n309:                 \"prompt\": prompt,\n310:                 \"profile\": profile,\n311:             },\n312:             wait_seconds=wait_seconds,\n313:         )\n314: \n315: \n316: class _Jobs(_Namespace):\n317:     def get(\n318:         self,\n319:         job_id: str,\n320:         *,\n321:         output: str | None = None,\n322:         include: list[str] | None = None,\n323:     ) -> Any:\n324:         \"\"\"The job's status, and its parsed content once available.\n325: \n326:         `output` and `include` select the representation, exactly as on\n327:         parse.run — omitting them here would have made the job route able to\n328:         return only the server default, so a caller who asked for elements on\n329:         the original request could not retrieve them.\n330:         \"\"\"\n331:         return JobsApi(self._client._api_client).jobs_get(\n332:             job_id, output=output, include=include\n333:         )\n334: \n335:     def list(\n336:         self,\n337:         *,\n338:         cursor: str | None = None,\n339:         limit: int | None = None,\n340:         status: str | None = None,\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
